RLK
---

Minimal C99 library for 2D grid-based games and roguelikes.

Build:
  make                  # Build librlk.a
  make lint             # Static analysis (-Werror)
  make test             # Run unit tests
  make clean            # Remove build artifacts

Note: the Makefiles use BSD make. On Linux, use `bmake` or `pmake`
instead of GNU make.

Configuration:
  Copy config.mk.example to config.mk to customize CFLAGS or library paths.

Design:
  - Zero allocation: the lib never calls malloc/free; all buffers are
    caller-owned (doc/architecture.md, "Memory model").
  - Determinism: same seed + same build -> identical world, byte for byte
    (build flags enforced in Makefile.inc).

Documentation:
  doc/architecture.md   # Zones (base / domains / user land), memory model,
                        # determinism contract, recipes
  doc/conventions.md    # Naming rules

Headers:
  rlk.h                # Umbrella header (includes all of the below)

  Base — core:
    err.h              # Error codes (RLK_OK, RLK_E_INVALID, RLK_E_NOTFOUND)
    hash.h             # Deterministic 64-bit hashing
    fmath.h            # Math helpers (clamp, lerp, smoothstep, distances)
    noise.h            # Noise generation (value, perlin, fbm)

  Base — data (POD, caller-owned):
    geom.h             # Rect (region) + lattice (grid geometry on world)
    grid.h             # Coarse float grid with bilinear sampling
    mask.h             # Uint8 mask (weight, density, visibility) + constructors
    poi.h              # Points of Interest (anchor, bbox, type, seed)
    tilemap.h          # Tile grid over a world rect + tile props + line drawing

  Domain terrain:
    slope.h            # Slope from an elevation grid (Horn 3x3)
    drain.h            # Drainage: fill, D8 flow, accumulation, river SDF
    hydro.h            # Derived hydrology: slope, Strahler order, speed

  Domain nav:
    path.h             # A* pathfinding (integer costs, lattice window)

  Domain vision:
    fov.h              # Field of view (recursive shadowcasting)

  Domain worldgen — pipeline (wg):
    wg.h            # Noise-field terrain generation engine
    wg_region.h     # Voronoi region (macro-area) stage
    wg_drain.h      # Drain reading stage
    wg_hydro.h      # Hydro reading stage
    wg_relief.h     # Standardised elevation stage
    wg_rivers.h     # River projection stage
    wg_poi.h        # POI detection stage

  Domain worldgen — structure generators:
    ca.h               # Cellular Automata (caves)
    bsp.h              # Binary Space Partitioning (dungeons)

Demos:
  demo/demo_viewer.c         # Generic PXL viewer: demo_viewer [world|ca|bsp|nav] [seed]
  demo/demo_world.c          # World composition: tilemap_gen + POI loop (ca/bsp) + roads (terminal)
  demo/tilemap_gen.h/c       # Reusable fantasy map generator (noise + drain + wg + POI)
  demo/widget.h              # UI elements (text, button, menu, legend; header-only)
  demo/viewer.h              # View bricks (camera, minimap, input snapshot; header-only)
  demo/source.h              # Viewer source interface (POD + callbacks; header-only)
  demo/viewer_app.h          # Generic PXL viewer shell over a source (header-only)
  demo/src_world.h           # World source: tilemap_gen + modes/probes/overlays (header-only)
  demo/src_dungeon.h         # ca/bsp sources (header-only)
  demo/src_nav.h             # nav scenario source (header-only)

